## 2. Exhaustive Unicode scalar sweep (`0x0000..0x10FFFF`)

Verified `utf8_is_space`, `utf8_is_punct`, `utf8_encode` -> `utf8_iterate` round-trip, and `utf8_case_fold` (FNV-1a 64-bit digest over all changed code points and folded UTF-8 bytes) across all 1,114,112 code points (1,112,064 valid Unicode scalars) against independent `libutf8proc` (Unicode 15.1.0) oracle:

```
ORACLE:  spaces=21 puncts=8617 folded=1530 hash=17511232294085469129
NPK -O0: spaces=21 puncts=8617 folded=1530 hash=17511232294085469129
NPK -O2: spaces=21 puncts=8617 folded=1530 hash=17511232294085469129
```

Both `-O0` and `-O2` exited 0 and matched the oracle bit-for-bit.

## 3. Error-relay seam check (`utf8_encode`, `utf8_check`, `utf8_case_fold`)

Using a failing `cm_buffer` stub whose `buffer_put` and `buffer_putc` return `fail EFakeBuf;`:
- `npkc` reach analysis confirmed `cm_buffer.EFakeBuf` propagates through `cm_utf8` to `failsafe`.
- At runtime, `utf8_encode`, `utf8_check`, and `utf8_case_fold` each relayed `cm_buffer.EFakeBuf` unchanged at both `-O0` and `-O2`:

```
RELAY -O0 OK
RELAY -O2 OK
```

